<Article title="Privacy Policy" description="What Ohmetry collects and what it does not: calculator inputs stay in your browser, and analytics use no cookies." h1="Privacy Policy">
<h2>Calculators</h2>
<p>Calculators run in your browser. The values you enter are not sent to a server and are not stored.</p>

<h2>Analytics</h2>
<p>Ohmetry uses Cloudflare Web Analytics to count visits and see which pages are used. It does not use cookies, does not track you across sites, and does not build a profile of individual visitors. Cloudflare processes the request data; see the <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare privacy policy</a>.</p>

<h2>Hosting</h2>
<p>The site is served through Cloudflare, which processes standard request data such as IP address and browser type to deliver pages and protect against abuse.</p>

<h2>Email</h2>
<p>If you write to hello@ohmetry.com, the message and your address are used only to reply. If a mailing list is added later, the sign-up form will name the email provider, and you can unsubscribe from any message.</p>

<h2>Advertising</h2>
<p>Ohmetry does not currently show advertising. If that changes, this page will list the advertising partners and cookies, and visitors in the EU and UK will be asked for consent first.</p>

<p>Questions: <a href="/contact/">contact</a>.</p>
</Article>
